    "name": "📌 Runway API",
    "description": "### About Runway\n\n\"Runway is building foundational Real-World Intelligence that can understand, simulate and act in the world.\"\n\nRunway builds its own Gen video and image models and serves them through its own API. On the workspace overview it is listed under **Image & video**.\n\n### Prerequisites\n\n- Postman Account\n    \n- Runway Account: [https://dev.runway.com/](https://dev.runway.com/)\n    \n\n### Usage\n\n1. Create a fork\n    \n2. Update collection variables\n    \n3. Send requests\n\nStart with the 🚀 Get Started folder.\n\nAdd your key to your **Postman Vault** as `runway_api_key` (Vault icon in the footer, then **Add secret**, using that exact name). Requests read it as `{{vault:runway_api_key}}`, so your key never leaves your device.\n\n### Documentation\n\n- API: [https://docs.dev.runwayml.com/](https://docs.dev.runwayml.com/)\n    \n- Models: [https://dev.runway.com/models](https://dev.runway.com/models)\n\n### Notes\n\nGeneration endpoints are asynchronous: they return a task `id`; **Tasks / Get task** polls `temp.task_id` until `status` is `SUCCEEDED` or `FAILED`.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
